WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.969
Percentages make numbers easy to compare.

2
00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:08.031
In this lesson, you will learn to add a Percent Of column, add a

3
00:00:08.031 --> 00:00:12.369
Percentage column, and keep your table tidy by moving and removing columns.

4
00:00:12.369 --> 00:00:14.900
Let's do the math, without the math!

5
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.609
We start on the Add Column tab, with Units Sold selected.

6
00:00:20.609 --> 00:00:22.686
Open Standard, and choose Percent Of.

7
00:00:22.686 --> 00:00:27.880
It asks for a value, and shows each row as a percentage of that value.

8
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.623
I type a value and click OK.

9
00:00:38.623 --> 00:00:40.614
A new column, Percent Of, appears.

10
00:00:40.614 --> 00:00:45.260
Each row now shows units sold as a share of the number we entered.

11
00:00:54.300 --> 00:01:00.525
I move the new column next to Units Sold, so we can compare them side by side.

12
00:01:00.525 --> 00:01:01.989
Keep related columns together.

13
00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:03.820
It makes checking much easier.

14
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:18.660
The Scientific menu sits right beside Standard, with tools like Square Root, Power, Exponent, and Logarithm.

15
00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:19.795
Now, Percentage.

16
00:01:19.795 --> 00:01:24.204
It takes a percentage you enter and applies it to each value.

17
00:01:24.204 --> 00:01:28.980
For example, enter ten, and each row shows ten percent of its value.

18
00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.397
Changed your mind?

19
00:01:32.397 --> 00:01:35.321
Right click the column header and choose Remove.

20
00:01:35.321 --> 00:01:37.880
Or delete the step in Applied Steps.

21
00:01:56.300 --> 00:02:01.453
Here I clean up the Percent Of column and check the remaining columns:

22
00:02:01.453 --> 00:02:05.020
Units Sold, Manufacturing Price, Sale Price, and Gross Sales.

23
00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.897
Next, I try Percentage on Profit.

24
00:02:23.897 --> 00:02:27.360
I select Profit, open Standard, and choose Percentage.

25
00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.941
Percent Of can also use another column as the base.

26
00:02:59.941 --> 00:03:05.767
Click the small icon next to Value, and pick a column from the list, like Sales.

27
00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:08.680
Now each row compares two columns. Very powerful!

